---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Comparison from '../components/Comparison.astro';
import PageCTA from '../components/PageCTA.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="txttoimage vs Convertio & More — Honest Comparison | txttoimage"
  description="Compare txttoimage vs Convertio, FreeConvert, Filestack. Privacy, pricing, speed, customization. Find which text-to-image converter is right for your needs."
  path="/compare"
>
  <section class="min-h-[50dvh] flex flex-col pt-28 pb-12">
    <div class="flex-1 flex flex-col max-w-3xl mx-auto w-full px-4">
      <p class="text-sm text-emerald-600 font-medium mb-3"><a href="/" class="hover:underline">txttoimage</a> &rsaquo; Compare</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 leading-[1.15]">txttoimage vs Alternatives — An Honest Comparison</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">A detailed, unbiased comparison of the most popular online text-to-image conversion tools. See how txttoimage stacks up against FreeConvert, Convertio, Aspose, and CloudConvert on privacy, features, pricing, speed, and user experience.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="py-4 bg-white border-b border-zinc-200 sticky top-14 z-40">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 flex items-center gap-1.5 overflow-x-auto">
      <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-400 uppercase tracking-wider mr-2 shrink-0">On this page:</span>
      <a href="#comparison-table" class="shrink-0 text-xs text-zinc-500 hover:text-emerald-600 bg-zinc-50 hover:bg-emerald-50 border border-zinc-200 hover:border-emerald-200 rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 transition-colors">Comparison</a>
      <a href="#privacy" class="shrink-0 text-xs text-zinc-500 hover:text-emerald-600 bg-zinc-50 hover:bg-emerald-50 border border-zinc-200 hover:border-emerald-200 rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 transition-colors">Privacy</a>
      <a href="#breakdown" class="shrink-0 text-xs text-zinc-500 hover:text-emerald-600 bg-zinc-50 hover:bg-emerald-50 border border-zinc-200 hover:border-emerald-200 rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 transition-colors">Breakdown</a>
      <a href="#decision" class="shrink-0 text-xs text-zinc-500 hover:text-emerald-600 bg-zinc-50 hover:bg-emerald-50 border border-zinc-200 hover:border-emerald-200 rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 transition-colors">Decision Guide</a>
      <a href="#faq" class="shrink-0 text-xs text-zinc-500 hover:text-emerald-600 bg-zinc-50 hover:bg-emerald-50 border border-zinc-200 hover:border-emerald-200 rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 transition-colors">FAQ</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <section id="comparison-table" class="py-8">
    <Comparison />
  </section>

  <section id="privacy" class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-zinc-900 tracking-tight">The Privacy Difference: Client-Side vs Server-Based</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">Every other tool in this comparison requires uploading your files to their servers for processing. This is the fundamental architectural difference — and it matters more than most people realize.</p>

      <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-emerald-50 border border-emerald-200 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-emerald-800 text-base">txttoimage — Client-Side</h3>
          <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm text-emerald-700">
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500 shrink-0">&check;</span> File read locally by browser</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500 shrink-0">&check;</span> Rendered on local HTML5 Canvas</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500 shrink-0">&check;</span> Zero network transmission of file content</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500 shrink-0">&check;</span> No server to compromise or subpoena</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500 shrink-0">&check;</span> Works offline after page load</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-red-800 text-base">Traditional Converters — Server-Side</h3>
          <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm text-red-700">
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-red-400 shrink-0">&times;</span> File uploaded to remote server</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-red-400 shrink-0">&times;</span> Processed in third-party cloud infrastructure</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-red-400 shrink-0">&times;</span> Data traverses network — potential interception</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-red-400 shrink-0">&times;</span> Server logs may retain file data</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-red-400 shrink-0">&times;</span> Requires internet connection</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 p-5 bg-zinc-50 border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 text-sm">Why this matters for real use cases</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">If you are converting proprietary source code, confidential business documents, legal contracts, financial reports, or client data — uploading to a third-party server is a genuine risk. Most converter services state they delete files after processing, but there is no way to verify this. With client-side processing, you do not need to trust anyone — your data physically never leaves your device. For companies with SOC 2, HIPAA, or GDPR compliance requirements, this distinction is critical.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="breakdown" class="py-16 bg-zinc-100">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-zinc-900 tracking-tight">Detailed Competitor Analysis</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">A deeper look at each major alternative, their strengths, and their limitations.</p>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6">
        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 text-lg">txttoimage vs FreeConvert</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">FreeConvert is one of the most popular multi-format converters, supporting hundreds of format pairs including text-to-image. It has a polished interface and broad format support. However, all files are uploaded to FreeConvert's servers for processing. The free tier limits uploads to 25MB per file total, and conversion speed depends on queue length and server load. Ads are displayed on the free tier, with a paid plan removing them. <strong>Winner for privacy and unlimited use:</strong> txttoimage. <strong>Winner for format breadth beyond text:</strong> FreeConvert.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 text-lg">txttoimage vs Convertio</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">Convertio offers a clean, modern user experience with support for a very wide range of file conversions. However, the free tier enforces a daily conversion limit and some features require account registration. Files are processed on Convertio's cloud servers. The paid plans unlock higher limits and priority processing. <strong>Winner for privacy and no-account access:</strong> txttoimage. <strong>Winner for non-text format conversions:</strong> Convertio.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 text-lg">txttoimage vs Aspose</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">Aspose is an enterprise document processing platform with powerful APIs for developers. Its free online conversion tools add watermarks to output files, and watermark-free output requires registration and potentially paid licensing. All processing is server-side. Aspose is better suited for enterprise API integration scenarios. <strong>Winner for simple, watermark-free conversion:</strong> txttoimage. <strong>Winner for programmatic API access:</strong> Aspose.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 text-lg">txttoimage vs CloudConvert</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">CloudConvert is a robust, API-first conversion platform with excellent reliability and broad format coverage. It offers 25 free conversions per day. Files are processed server-side. CloudConvert is a strong choice if you need a reliable paid conversion API. <strong>Winner for privacy and unlimited free use:</strong> txttoimage. <strong>Winner for API reliability and format depth:</strong> CloudConvert.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="decision" class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-zinc-900 tracking-tight">Which Converter Should You Choose?</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">Your choice depends on what matters most to you. Here is a decision guide based on different priorities.</p>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-4">
        <div class="bg-emerald-50 border border-emerald-200 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-emerald-800">Choose txttoimage if you value...</h3>
          <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm text-emerald-700">
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500 shrink-0">&rarr;</span> Privacy — your files never leave your device</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500 shrink-0">&rarr;</span> No limits — unlimited free conversions forever</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500 shrink-0">&rarr;</span> Customization — full control over fonts, colors, padding, and aspect ratio</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500 shrink-0">&rarr;</span> Speed — no upload wait, instant local rendering</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500 shrink-0">&rarr;</span> Simplicity — no registration, no ads, no paywalls</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-zinc-50 border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-800">Choose another tool if you need...</h3>
          <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm text-zinc-600">
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-zinc-400 shrink-0">&rarr;</span> Non-text format conversion (PDF, DOCX, images, video)</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-zinc-400 shrink-0">&rarr;</span> A REST API for automated server-side conversion workflows</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-zinc-400 shrink-0">&rarr;</span> Batch conversion of many files simultaneously</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-zinc-400 shrink-0">&rarr;</span> Output formats beyond PNG, JPG, and WebP (like PDF, SVG, TIFF)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="faq" class="py-16 bg-zinc-100">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-zinc-900 tracking-tight">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <dl class="mt-8 space-y-1">
        <details class="group bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl">
          <summary class="px-5 py-4 cursor-pointer font-medium text-zinc-900 text-sm flex items-center justify-between">Is txttoimage really free with no catches? <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform ml-2 shrink-0" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">Yes. There is no paid tier, no premium plan, no daily conversion limit, no watermarking, and no registration requirement. This is possible because all processing happens in your browser — txttoimage does not incur server costs per conversion. The only practical limit is the 10MB file size cap, which is a browser memory safety measure, not a business restriction. We do not even run ads.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="group bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl">
          <summary class="px-5 py-4 cursor-pointer font-medium text-zinc-900 text-sm flex items-center justify-between">Why should I trust txttoimage with my files? <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform ml-2 shrink-0" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">You do not need to trust us — that is the point. Because all processing is client-side, your files never reach any server we control. You can verify this yourself: open your browser's Developer Tools, go to the Network tab, and you will see that no file data is ever transmitted after the page loads. The converter works entirely within your browser using standard Web APIs (FileReader, Canvas). We could not access your files even if we wanted to.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="group bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl">
          <summary class="px-5 py-4 cursor-pointer font-medium text-zinc-900 text-sm flex items-center justify-between">Does txttoimage have fewer features than paid converters? <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform ml-2 shrink-0" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">For text-to-image conversion specifically, txttoimage has <strong>more</strong> customization features than most paid alternatives. You can customize font family (8 options including JetBrains Mono and Fira Code), font size (10px to 32px), bold/italic, background and text colors, padding, and aspect ratio (7 options including Auto Fit). Most paid converters only offer basic DPI or resize options for text-to-image conversion. Where paid tools excel is in non-text format conversion (PDF, DOCX, video, audio) and batch API processing — these are not the focus of txttoimage.</div>
        </details>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wide">Related Pages</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/txt-to-png" class="text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-full px-4 py-2 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-600 transition-colors">TXT to PNG</a>
        <a href="/txt-to-jpg" class="text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-full px-4 py-2 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-600 transition-colors">TXT to JPG</a>
        <a href="/code-to-image" class="text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-full px-4 py-2 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-600 transition-colors">Code to Image</a>
        <a href="/how-it-works" class="text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-full px-4 py-2 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-600 transition-colors">How It Works</a>
        <a href="/" class="text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-full px-4 py-2 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-600 transition-colors">Home</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <PageCTA title="Experience the Difference Yourself" description="Try txttoimage and see why client-side processing is the better way to convert text to images. No uploads, no sign-up, instant results." buttonText="Try txttoimage Free" />

  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is txttoimage really free with no catches?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. There is no paid tier, no premium plan, no daily conversion limit, no watermarking, and no registration requirement. This is possible because all processing happens in your browser — txttoimage does not incur server costs per conversion."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why should I trust txttoimage with my files?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You do not need to trust us. Because all processing is client-side, your files never reach any server. You can verify this in your browser's Developer Tools Network tab — no file data is ever transmitted after the page loads."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does txttoimage have fewer features than paid converters?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For text-to-image conversion specifically, txttoimage has more customization features than most paid alternatives: font family, font size, colors, padding, and aspect ratio. Most paid converters only offer basic DPI or resize options."}}]}
  </script>
</Layout>
